IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pa08-types`
IMPORT `pa08-status`
IMPORT `pa08-penalties`

-- Pensions Act 2008 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Workplace pension case` HAS
    `the worker`                                        IS A `Worker facts`
    `the pay reference period`                          IS A `Pay reference period`
    `the contributions`                                 IS A MAYBE `Contributions`
    `the penalties`                                     IS A MAYBE `Penalty facts`

DECLARE `Workplace pension position` HAS
    `status`                                            IS A `Pension status`
    `qualifying earnings`                               IS A NUMBER
    `minimum employer contribution`                     IS A NUMBER
    `minimum total contribution`                        IS A NUMBER
    `contributions meet the quality requirement`        IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `earliest fixed penalty payment date`               IS A MAYBE DATE
    `fixed penalty within the limit`                    IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `escalating penalty`                                IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref ss 1, 3, 7, 9, 13, 20, 40, 41
@export default The position under the Pensions Act 2008 (UK) for one worker and one pay reference period: their status (automatic enrolment, may opt in, may ask to join, or outside the duties); their qualifying earnings and the minimum employer (3%) and total (8%) contributions; whether given contributions meet the s 20 quality requirement; and, for penalty notices, the earliest fixed penalty payment date, whether the fixed penalty is within £50,000, and the escalating penalty. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Workplace pension case`  @desc The worker, the pay reference period, any contributions, and any penalty notice facts
GIVETH A `Workplace pension position`
`the workplace pension position for` c MEANS
    `Workplace pension position` WITH
        `status`                                        IS `the pension status of` (c's `the worker`) `in` p
        `qualifying earnings`                           IS qe
        `minimum employer contribution`                 IS 0.03 TIMES qe
        `minimum total contribution`                    IS 0.08 TIMES qe
        `contributions meet the quality requirement`    IS
            CONSIDER c's `the contributions`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN JUST (`the contributions meet the quality requirement in` p `with` k)
        `earliest fixed penalty payment date`           IS
            CONSIDER c's `the penalties`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST f  THEN JUST (`the earliest payment date for` f)
        `fixed penalty within the limit`                IS
            CONSIDER c's `the penalties`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST f  THEN JUST (`the fixed penalty is within the limit in` f)
        `escalating penalty`                            IS
            CONSIDER c's `the penalties`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST f  THEN JUST (`the escalating penalty under` f)
    WHERE
        p MEANS c's `the pay reference period`
        qe MEANS `the qualifying earnings in` p
